# Control UI contracts

Full framework: [`docs/Control_UI.md`](../../docs/Control_UI.md).

## OBS canvas

`html, body { background: transparent }` — never paint an opaque page fill. Operator
chrome (guides, checkerboard, crosshairs) renders only under `body.settings-mode`.
ABS apps omit the checkerboard util — the canvas is the backdrop.

## Live update — imperative

Every setting change does **both**, in the **same** handler. No Save, no reload.

```js
slider.addEventListener('input', (e) => {   // 'input', not 'change'/blur
  state.radius = Number(e.target.value);
  applyToPage(state);                       // running render path updates now
  updateURL();                              // rewrite query (omit defaults)
});

function updateURL() {
  const search = buildSearchParams(state).toString();
  history.replaceState({}, "", search ? "?" + search : location.pathname);
}
```

## Sliders

Range controls should include a per-param **↺** reset (`.reset-param` + `data-reset`),
as in Sesh Banner and Diamond — next to the value readout.

## URL is the entire config

No `localStorage`, no account, no config server. Every persisted setting has a short,
stable query param. On load: parse params, hydrate state, sync UI, apply to page;
missing params fall back to defaults. **When writing**, omit any param that matches
its effective default. Free-text content params (`title`, `user`, `message`,
`playlist`, `prefix`, …) go **last** in a fixed per-app order. Booleans are
`"true"` / `"false"`. Runtime-only controls (Test / Preview) get no param but still
update the page live.

Copy URL is `navigator.clipboard.writeText(location.href)`. **Copy URL for OBS**
rebuilds via the same `buildSearchParams` helper with `menu=DISABLE` — do not
append `menu` onto the live query string.

## Visibility

Minimum params are `menu` (`DISABLE` hides the panel and overlays) and `side`
(`left` | `right`, apps default to right). Double-click on the background only *shows*
the menu; only `✕` or `menu=DISABLE` hides it. Clicks inside `#settings-menu` never
reach the background handler.

## Before claiming done

Drag a slider → effect changes → URL changes → copy → open in a new tab → matches.
Document app-specific params in that app's `notes.md`, not in `Control_UI.md`.
